course: dictionary
lesson: 13296
title: Gratified: pleased and satisfied
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Gratified is a formal word for pleased. You feel gratified when something has gone well, or when someone has praised you for something you did.
explain: «The coach was gratified to hear that everyone had passed the test.» The clue is the good news. The coach felt pleased because the result was good, so gratified means pleased and satisfied.
explain: Gratified can also show pride. In a story, a character who is gratified by praise may feel very proud of himself. Look at the clues around the word to see whether the pride is happy or too big.
fact: Gratified is an adjective. It often goes with «to» or «by»: gratified to hear, gratified by the result.
fact: «Gratified» means pleased and satisfied, especially after something has gone well or someone has praised you.
fact: Gratify is a verb. «The gift gratified her wish for a puppy» means the gift satisfied her wish.
fact: «Gratifying» means giving pleasure, as in «a gratifying result».
fact: Gratified is a formal word. In everyday speech, pleased or happy usually works just as well.
exercise: «The class was gratified by the kind words from the head teacher.» What does gratified mean here? | Angry and cross | Bored and tired | Lost and confused | *Pleased and satisfied
exercise: «Ali was gratified to win the race.» Which clue tells you why Ali felt pleased? | He lost his bag | His lunch was late | *He had trained hard all year | The sky was grey
exercise: Mum was ___ when the whole family tidied the kitchen without being asked. Choose the best word. | hungry | sleepy | frightened | *gratified
test: «The author was gratified by the excellent reviews of her book.» Gratified means | Tired of writing | Worried about the cost of printing | *Pleased because of the praise | Confused by the words
test: «She was gratified by the result.» Which everyday word could replace gratified here? | cold | *pleased | sorry | lost
exam: Which sentence uses gratified correctly? | «My shoes are gratified with mud.» | *«Dad was gratified when we tidied the garden without being asked.» | «The rain was gratified by the sunshine.» | «The bus was gratified at the station.»
